- op: discuss  # d160
  at: '2026-08-04T19:29:35Z'  # d160
  by: agent  # d160
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d160
  clock: 3  # d160
  nonce: d160  # d160
  message: "CROSS-LINK from PR #204 (INV-karud clause a3). The published dataflow_coverage block now emits a declared constant coverage_granularity = \"language\", whose stated meaning is that capability is reported PER LANGUAGE and is explicitly NOT a per-function completeness claim -- cfg_nodes/go.yaml self-documents that \"if err := do(); err != nil\" initializers are invisible to def/use, so a language marked dataflow_capable still holds functions the walk cannot see into.\n\nThis item is the finer signal. When the coverage gate lands (forfeit refutation for any function whose CFG statement extents miss a call node in its body), that per-function bit is exactly what the scope block should report, and the constant becomes \"function\". Its test asserts the current value, so the change cannot be forgotten silently -- the assertion fails until it is updated, which is the executable re-evaluation trigger R16 asks for.\n\nNo change to this item scope or priority. Recorded so the two are not worked independently."  # d160
- op: discuss  # da9a
  at: '2026-08-06T09:03:11Z'  # da9a
  by: agent  # da9a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # da9a
  clock: 4  # da9a
  nonce: da9a  # da9a
  message: "MEASUREMENT TAKEN, as this item asked. Instrument ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/meas/forfeit_share.py; log forfeit_share.log. It mirrors ddg_build._solve_one_function exactly (same registered LanguageDdgSpec, same build_function_cfg / populate_def_use_for_cfg / solve_reaching_defs) and then asks production cfg.uncovered_call_lines of each function, so nothing is re-derived. POSITIVE CONTROL passes in BOTH directions: a known-uncovered if-initializer reports exactly one site, and the same code with the initializer hoisted reports zero. DENOMINATOR is functions that PRODUCE DDG EDGES - the only population section 3a can act on; functions with no edges are reported separately, never folded in. RESULT, five repo-language pairs: alertmanager/go 445 of 1329 = 33.5%; prometheus/go 1696 of 4773 = 35.5%; kserve/go 470 of 1747 = 26.9%; kserve/python 420 of 1512 = 27.8%; hypergumbo/python 3164 of 24769 = 12.8%. NOT NEAR 100 PERCENT. By this item own pre-registered reading that means refutation IS viable on the remainder - roughly two thirds to seven eighths of walkable functions - rather than the substrate being unusable. CORRECTION TO MY OWN FIRST RUN, recorded because it nearly shipped: the first python figure was 21.5% over 158,088 walkable functions. The instrument was sweeping a virtualenv, so a large part of that share was a statement about third-party code rather than this repo. Excludes widened (.venv, venv, site-packages, .tox, build, dist, caches) and the first-party figure is 24,769 functions at 12.8%. Read the earlier number as void. WHAT LANDED: _ddg_taint_reaches gains forfeit_refutation (default False, so no existing caller changes behaviour) and cfg.uncovered_call_lines computes the evidence. Blocks False only, never True - a True is positive evidence an incomplete picture cannot unmake, and downgrading it would turn a safety gate into a recall regression. THE GATE IS NOT YET WIRED INTO PRODUCTION; nothing passes forfeit_refutation=True. Measuring before wiring was deliberate - the share is what decides whether wiring is worth it and the pre-state is unrecoverable afterwards. ALSO CORRECTED: this item SEQUENCING paragraph claimed it is behaviour-neutral today because the sole production call site is a True test. That has been stale since PR #214 gave False a second consumer (the barrier arm earns sanitized on False and a sanitized flow is dropped from a claim violation set). The correction was recorded on WI-kabif and never applied here; it is applied now."  # da9a
- op: discuss  # f17b
  at: '2026-08-06T10:44:16Z'  # f17b
  by: agent  # f17b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f17b
  clock: 5  # f17b
  nonce: f17b  # f17b
  message: "GATE NOW WIRED, and its measured effect is ZERO - reported as a CLOSED ROUTE, not an improvement. RepoDdg carries forfeit_refutation; build_repo_ddg populates it, _build_ddg_for_verify_claims threads it, propagate_taint_ddg consults it. WIRED ON ONE ARM ONLY: the section 3a arm tests is True so False and None already collapse there and the gate cannot alter it. The barrier arm is where a False earns sanitized and a sanitized flow is dropped from the claim violation set, so that is the arm that got the gate. DIRECTION: strictly fewer suppressions, hence strictly MORE surviving violations - which is why this could land before removal authority exists. MEASURED DELTA ZERO: alertmanager yields 59 evidence rows, all ddg_mixed, 0 sanitized. The gate can only turn sanitized into not-sanitized, so with zero sanitized findings it provably changed nothing. Same shape as WI-votom - a route closed before anything could walk it wrongly. This independently corroborates INV-karud clause (b) 0-registered-sanitizer-call-sites finding on fresh substrate: the shipped sanitizer vocabulary is crypto-only (go 1, python 4, rust 3, typescript 3, javascript 0). 445 of alertmanager 1329 walkable functions DO forfeit, so the moment a barrier registers inside one of them the gate bites. CROSS-CHECK: production build_repo_ddg reproduces the standalone instrument counts exactly (445 of 1329), so the measurement and the shipped path agree rather than being two implementations of one idea. THE FORFEIT POPULATION DIFFERS BY LANGUAGE AND WAS READ, NOT ASSUMED. Go forfeits on the if-initializer its own cfg_nodes/go.yaml self-documents. PYTHON FORFEITS ON A DIFFERENT SHAPE ENTIRELY: the call in a for-x-in-CALL iterable and in a with-CALL-as-f context-manager header. My first non-vacuity test reasoned by analogy from Go and used a call inside an if test - that forfeits NOTHING in python, because the if condition contains its calls. This is why python measures 12.8% against go 33.5%: the languages fail in DIFFERENT PLACES, and it is the strongest evidence yet that coverage-gating rather than gap-enumeration was the right design - a gap list would have shipped with Go case handled and Python invisible. NOTE FOR THE ESCAPE-RECLASSIFICATION WORK: these python sites are GENUINE coverage gaps, not misclassified escapes. for-x-in-CALL and with-CALL-as-f both BIND a value, so data really does flow where the DDG cannot see. They are not candidates for the expression-read reclassification, which targets assert/binary/return/defer where nothing is stored. Do not let that work quietly absorb them."  # f17b
- op: discuss  # cfa7
  at: '2026-08-06T17:21:07Z'  # cfa7
  by: agent  # cfa7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cfa7
  clock: 6  # cfa7
  nonce: cfa7  # cfa7
  message: "THE GATE'S MEASURED ZERO NOW HAS A STRUCTURAL EXPLANATION, NOT JUST AN\nEMPIRICAL ONE. Measured 2026-08-06 across four repos with a wrapper reading the\narm directly off barrier_lines:\n\n    repo          walk invocations   3a arm   BARRIER arm\n    hypergumbo          36             36          0\n    pretix              35             35          0\n    prometheus           7              7          0\n    alertmanager         3              3          0\n\nZERO barrier-arm walks anywhere. This item's gate is wired to the sanitizer\narm only -- correctly, since the 3a arm tests \"is True\" and collapses\nFalse/None -- so the gate provably cannot fire on this corpus. The delta was\nreported as zero when it landed; this is WHY, and it is a property of the\npipeline rather than a property of alertmanager.\n\nMECHANISM. The barrier arm runs only when 3a already returned True AND the\nsource function calls a catalogued sanitizer (barrier_sites non-empty). The\nshipped sanitizer vocabulary is crypto-only, so a barrier registers only where\na repo calls a crypto primitive in the same function as a taint source. This\ncorroborates INV-karud clause (b)'s \"0 registered sanitizer call sites across\n95,950 taint call edges\" from the opposite direction -- measured at the WALK\nrather than at the edge index, on four repos rather than one.\n\nWHY THIS STRENGTHENS RATHER THAN WEAKENS THE ITEM. The filing argued \"build the\ngate BEFORE removal authority, not after\". The measurement says the arm the\ngate protects has no live traffic at all -- so the gate is a closed route in\nfront of a road nobody drives yet. That is exactly the position the filing\nwanted: the protection is in place before the traffic arrives, and the cost of\nhaving built it early is zero because nothing regressed.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE FORFEIT SHARE. 445 of alertmanager's 1,329 walkable\nfunctions forfeit, and 12.8-35.5% across languages -- but zero of those\nforfeits can currently change a verdict, because forfeit_refutation blocks\nFalse and no consumer reads False. Recorded so the forfeit share is not later\ncited as evidence that the gate is doing work; it is evidence that the gate\nWOULD do work."  # cfa7
- op: discuss  # e11c
  at: '2026-08-06T18:30:16Z'  # e11c
  by: agent  # e11c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e11c
  clock: 7  # e11c
  nonce: e11c  # e11c
  message: "CORRECTION to my note above, same day. I wrote that this gate 'guards a\nroad nobody drives' and attributed the empty road to a crypto-only\nsanitizer vocabulary. The road is empty for a different reason.\n\nWHAT I CLAIMED, HOURS EARLIER TODAY: zero barrier-arm walks BECAUSE the\nshipped sanitizer vocabulary is crypto-only -- and therefore \"a sanitizer\ncatalogue ARMS the removal hazard; catalogue growth creates the danger, so\ngates land before catalogue growth.\"\n\nWHY IT WAS NOT ESTABLISHED: I never positive-controlled the zero. A null\nbelieved without demonstrating the instrument can produce a known positive is\nthe exact rule this repo has written down, and I violated it the same day I\nedited it into LIVE.md. It is also the shape of this area's own invalidated\n0.00% confident-negative figure: a tautology of the configuration.\n\nTWO PURPOSE-BUILT FIXTURES, BOTH ZERO WALKS:\n  v1  f = Fernet(key); plain = f.decrypt(tok); cipher = f.encrypt(plain);\n      pathlib.Path(...).write_text(cipher)\n      -> the crypto calls emit python:external:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol.\n         The receiver type is never inferred, so the SOURCE cannot match\n         cryptography.fernet.Fernet.decrypt and the SANITIZER cannot match\n         Fernet.encrypt. No flow exists for a barrier to guard.\n  v2  the same shape written MODULE-QUALIFIED, removing receiver typing as a\n      variable -> source and sanitizer now resolve\n      (python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol), but the\n      SINK emits NO call edge at all: pathlib.Path(...).write_text(x) is an\n      attribute chain rooted at a CONSTRUCTOR RESULT. Still zero walks.\n\nSO THE BARRIER ARM IS UNREACHABLE FOR THE SAME ROOT CAUSE AS THE REST OF THIS\nAREA. Every sanitizer in the shipped catalogue is an INSTANCE METHOD --\nFernet.encrypt, AESGCM.encrypt, AEAD.Seal, Cipher.doFinal -- and\ninstance-method receiver typing is precisely what is broken (INV-linub). That\nis a THIRD symptom family from one root cause, alongside io-boundary catalogue\nreach and the section 4 summary lookup inside the walk.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES: the observation (0 barrier walks across 4 repos and 2 fixtures)\nand the practical verdict (an escape reclassification cannot move a finding\ntoday). WHAT DOES NOT: the mechanism, and every sequencing conclusion built on\nit. Catalogue growth CANNOT arm the hazard while receiver typing is broken.\nRECEIVER TYPING IS WHAT ARMS IT.\n\nSTILL OPEN, stated rather than papered over: I could not construct a barrier\nwalk in ANY configuration, so I cannot distinguish \"reachable, and nothing in\nthe corpus hits it\" from \"effectively dead on the DDG path\". There is also NO\nend-to-end test driving the barrier arm through propagate_taint_ddg -- the one\n'sanitized' test uses propagate_taint_structural. A positive control is a\nprerequisite for any future claim about this arm, mine included.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THIS ITEM, AND IT IS FAVOURABLE. The gate protects the\nFalse path on the barrier arm. That arm becomes reachable when RECEIVER\nTYPING is fixed (INV-linub), not when the sanitizer catalogue grows. So\nthe gate is already in place BEFORE the change that will switch the\ntraffic on -- which is exactly the order this item's filing demanded\n('build the gate BEFORE removal authority, not after'), and it holds for\na sharper reason than the one I gave: the arming event is a specific,\nalready-filed, already-blocking class item rather than a diffuse\ncatalogue-growth trend.\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR VALIDATING THE GATE. Its measured delta stays zero\nand cannot be validated on findings until INV-linub lands. The forfeit\nshare (12.8-35.5%) is evidence the gate WOULD act, not that it does.\nThe right validation point is immediately after receiver typing lands,\nwith an A/B on the gate across the same cohort -- and that A/B is now a\ngenuine safety check rather than a formality, because it is the first\nmoment an unearned False can suppress a real finding."  # e11c
- op: discuss  # 5263
  at: '2026-08-06T22:05:02Z'  # 5263
  by: agent  # 5263
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5263
  clock: 8  # 5263
  nonce: '5263'  # 5263
  message: "BARRIER-ARM MECHANISM CORRECTED A SECOND TIME, 2026-08-06 (dev 8b1a20cc1b,\nfiled as INV-funit). This thread carries a correction from earlier the same\nday saying \"receiver typing arms the suppression hazard, not catalogue\ngrowth\". THAT IS ALSO WRONG and is retracted; it was the second uncontrolled\naccount of the same zero.\n\nESTABLISHED WITH A POSITIVE CONTROL, which neither prior account had: the\nbarrier arm was blocked by _register_sanitizer_callers reading the NAME slot\nof the dst for receiver evidence that production analyzers put in the MODULE\nslot. The comparison was \"cryptography.fernet.Fernet.encrypt\" == \"encrypt\" --\nfalse by construction for every method-shaped sanitizer, i.e. the entire\nshipped catalogue -- so the INV-finoh call_construct==\"method\" refusal was\nunconditional in production.\n\nTwo probes differing ONLY in receiver form emit a BYTE-IDENTICAL dst\n(python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:encrypt:external_symbol) and differ\nonly in meta.call_construct; that alone flipped sanitizer_lines from\n{(handler,'plaintext'): [7,7,7,7]} to {}. The idiomatic form reported\n\"violated\" at \"precise\" confidence about code that visibly encrypts, and now\nreports \"confirmed\" with the arm firing.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES FROM BOTH RETRACTED ACCOUNTS: WI-joluk's coverage gate landing\nbefore removal authority is still right. The section 3a arm still tests\n`is True`, so escape-reclassification and section 7a field sensitivity are\nstill structurally INERT for finding counts. INV-karud clause (b)'s zero is\nstill not independent corroboration.\n\nWHAT IS NEW AND DECISION-RELEVANT: the corpus holds ZERO plaintext sanitizer\ncall sites (pretix's single gate-reaching edge is a bare `encrypt`, correctly\nrefused; everywhere else is absence), and the module slot reaches taint only\nfor python and java. The sanitizer/barrier machinery has no live surface on\ntoday's corpus -- everything here is prevention whose value scales with a\ncatalogue that is not growing. That belongs in the exit-condition package."  # 5263
- op: update  # e4d4
  at: '2026-08-10T02:41:33Z'  # e4d4
  by: agent  # e4d4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e4d4
  clock: 9  # e4d4
  nonce: e4d4  # e4d4
  set:  # e4d4
    description: "STATUS IN ONE LINE, BECAUSE THIS ITEM READS AS UNSTARTED AND IS NOT: the gate is\nBUILT, TESTED and WIRED TO THE BARRIER ARM. What remains is the section 3a arm,\ndeliberately deferred. (De-staled 2026-08-09; a session status report described this\nitem as \"unstarted\" on the strength of its todo_hard status, which was wrong.)\n\n  BUILT     cfg.uncovered_call_lines (cfg.py:1457) -- call sites in a function's AST\n            body that no recorded CFG statement covers.\n  BUILT     _ddg_taint_reaches(..., forfeit_refutation=False) (taint.py:2034, logic at\n            2326) -- downgrades a would-be False to None. Blocks False ONLY, never\n            True: a True is positive evidence an incomplete picture cannot unmake.\n  WIRED     the BARRIER arm (taint.py:2792) passes it.\n  NOT WIRED the section 3a arm passes nothing, so a partially-recorded definition can\n            still yield False there.\n\nWIRING THE SECTION 3a ARM TODAY IS A NO-OP AND MUST NOT BE DONE ALONE. That arm tests\n`is True`, so False -> None changes nothing, and 0 of 68 production section 3a walks\nreturn False at all. Land it IN THE SAME PR as any grant of section 3a removal\nauthority -- since PR #214 an unearned False DELETES a flow, so the ordering is\nload-bearing, and WI-kabif (removal authority) is explicitly not to be started.\n\nFORFEIT SHARE, the number that decided the gate was worth building: 12.8% - 35.5%\nacross five repo-language pairs (alertmanager/go 33.5%, prometheus/go 35.5%,\nkserve/go 26.9%, kserve/python 27.8%, hypergumbo/python 12.8%). Not near 100%, so by\nthis item's own pre-registered reading refutation stays viable on the remainder.\n\n---- ORIGINAL FILING BELOW, with two corrections applied inline ----\n\nTHE STRUCTURAL FIX BEHIND INV-lupav. PR #199 closed the acute case -- a definition the\nDDG holds NO entry for now yields None instead of False. It did not close the class,\nand the residual is verified live on merged dev:\n\n    L1  v := source()\n    L2  w := f(v)                  <- recorded by def/use\n    L5  if n := sink(v); n > 0 {   <- use of v in an if-INITIALIZER, INVISIBLE\n\nCORRECTION 1 -- THE FILED REPRO NO LONGER RUNS AS WRITTEN. This description used to\ngive it as:\n\n    _ddg_taint_reaches(\"f\", [1], [5], {(\"f\",1):{2}, (\"f\",2):{1}})  ->  False\n\nRe-run on merged dev it returns None, not False -- because since PR #203 the ddg_uses\nkey is (symbol_id, variable, def_line) and seeding comes from defs_at, so the call\nabove never reaches the walk and returns None FOR THE WRONG REASON. Do not read that\nNone as the defect being fixed. The faithful repro (recorded on INV-lupav and\nre-verified there 2026-08-08 with all controls passing) needs defs_at seeding AND\ncallees_at AND production summaries:\n\n    defs_at={(f,1):{v}}, ddg_uses={(f,v,1):{2}}, callees_at={(f,2):{fmt.Printf}},\n    source_lines=[1], sink_lines=[5]\n      gate OFF -> False    gate ON -> None    control (use recorded) -> True\n\nA reconstruction that omits callees_at/summaries returns None in every arm INCLUDING\nthe positive control, which means the probe never reached the walk. That trap has now\ncaught two separate attempts; do not make it a third.\n\nEvery frontier line has an entry, so nothing is barren and nothing escapes. The walk\nreturns False -- the only verdict that may ever license removing a reported flow --\nfor a definition it did not follow at every step. The true answer is True: v IS an\nargument at the sink call site.\n\nWHY ENUMERATING GAPS CANNOT WORK. The population is whatever the def/use extractor\ndoes not model, per language, and that set is not knowable from inside the walk.\ncfg_nodes/go.yaml self-documents one instance (if_statement and for_clause\ninitializers); there is no reason to believe it is the only one, and the walk cannot\ntell a construct it was never taught about from one that genuinely has no uses. Any\nfix shaped as \"handle the known gaps\" is a list that decays silently.\n\nTHE GATE. Refutation must be COVERAGE-GATED rather than gap-enumerated: for the\nfunction under walk, compare the call nodes present in its AST body against the\nstatement extents the CFG recorded. If any call node falls outside every recorded\nextent, the extractor demonstrably did not see part of this function and refutation is\nforfeited for it.\n\nCORRECTION 2 -- THE \"BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL\" SEQUENCING CLAIM IS DELETED, NOT SOFTENED.\nThis description used to say \"SEQUENCING. Behaviour-neutral today: the sole production\ncall site is a True test.\" That has been FALSE since PR #214 gave False a second\nconsumer -- the barrier arm earns `sanitized` on a False, and a sanitized flow is\ndropped from a claim's violation set. The correction was recorded on WI-kabif, then on\nthis item's own thread on 2026-08-06, and the description text was never amended, so\nthe false sentence stayed in the field a reader sees first. It is removed here rather\nthan annotated, because a banner above a still-present falsehood is missable.\n\nSECOND RESIDUAL, unmeasured: cfg.uncovered_call_lines keys on CALL nodes only, so a\ndef/use omission at a NON-call construct is invisible to the gate. Read from\ncfg.py:1457; not measured."  # e4d4
- op: discuss  # 8a57
  at: '2026-08-10T02:41:48Z'  # 8a57
  by: agent  # 8a57
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8a57
  clock: 10  # 8a57
  nonce: 8a57  # 8a57
  message: "DESCRIPTION DE-STALED 2026-08-09. Three things were wrong in the field a reader\nhits first, and all three are now fixed IN the text rather than annotated above it:\n\n1. IT READ AS UNSTARTED AND IS NOT. The gate is built (cfg.uncovered_call_lines,\n   cfg.py:1457), tested, and wired to the BARRIER arm (taint.py:2792). Only the\n   section 3a arm is unwired, deliberately. A session status report to the owner\n   described this item as 'unstarted' on the strength of its todo_hard status --\n   that was my error and it came from reading the status field instead of the\n   thread. The description now leads with what is built.\n\n2. THE 'BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL TODAY' SEQUENCING CLAIM was false since PR #214 and was\n   corrected on this thread on 2026-08-06 -- but only in the thread. The\n   description kept saying it for three more days. DELETED from the text now, not\n   annotated, because a correction banner above a still-present falsehood is\n   missable and this particular falsehood licenses shipping an unearned False.\n\n3. THE FILED REPRO NO LONGER RUNS AS WRITTEN. Verified today: the description's\n   call returns None, not False, because the post-PR-#203 ddg_uses key is\n   (symbol_id, variable, def_line) with defs_at seeding, so it never reaches the\n   walk. A reader could easily read that None as 'fixed'. The faithful repro is now\n   in the description, together with the warning that omitting callees_at/summaries\n   returns None in EVERY arm including the positive control. I fell into exactly\n   that trap while checking this today, which is the second recorded instance.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED (todo_hard) and nothing here is closure evidence. Arguably the\nstatus overstates actionability, since the remaining work must land in the same PR\nas WI-kabif's removal authority and WI-kabif is explicitly not to be started --\nbut changing it is an owner call, not a de-staling edit, so it is left alone and\nflagged here."  # 8a57
